      "title": "Type-Level Programming: The Mental Model",
      "role": "outline",
      "outlineIndex": 0,
      "pages": [
        {
          "title": "Type-Level Programming: The Mental Model",
          "blocks": [
            {
              "type": "heading",
              "text": "1. Compile-Time Only",
              "ink": "green"
            },
            {
              "type": "bullets",
              "items": [
                "Template, mapped, conditional types are ==erased==",
                "They emit {red:no runtime code}",
                "A type is a function from types to types"
              ],
              "style": "dot",
              "frame": "dashed",
              "ink": "green"
            },
            {
              "type": "heading",
              "text": "2. The Four Tools",
              "ink": "blue"
            },
            {
              "type": "table",
              "headers": [
                "Tool",
                "Form",
                "Reads as"
              ],
              "rows": [
                [
                  "Template",
                  "`${A}${B}`",
                  "Union in a slot → every combination"
                ],
                [
                  "Mapped",
                  "`{ [K in Keys]: T }`",
                  "for-each over a union of keys"
                ],
                [
                  "Conditional",
                  "`T extends U ? X : Y`",
                  "if/else; distributes over naked union"
                ],
                [
                  "infer",
                  "`infer R`",
                  "captures the matched position"
                ]
              ]
            },
            {
              "type": "code",
              "lang": "typescript",
              "lines": [
                "type E = `${'a'|'b'}${1|2}`",
                "// 'a1'|'a2'|'b1'|'b2'",
                "type Ret<T> = T extends () => infer R ? R : never"
              ]
            },
            {
              "type": "heading",
              "text": "3. Distribution and infer",
              "ink": "purple"
            },
            {
              "type": "bullets",
              "items": [
                "Only a ==naked== `T` distributes over a union",
                "`[T] extends [U]` turns distribution off",
                "`infer R` lives only in the `extends` clause",
                "R captures whatever matches that slot"
              ],
              "style": "check"
            },
            {
              "type": "callout",
              "style": "sticky",
              "title": "Remember",
              "text": "Nothing here exists at runtime: no value, no code."
            }
          ]
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "title": "Template Literal Types and String Intrinsics",
      "role": "outline",
      "outlineIndex": 1,
      "pages": [
        {
          "title": "Template Literal Types and String Intrinsics",
          "blocks": [
            {
              "type": "heading",
              "text": "1. Building string types",
              "ink": "green"
            },
            {
              "type": "bullets",
              "items": [
                "`on${'click'|'hover'}` gives `'onclick'|'onhover'`",
                "Two unions of sizes m and n give ==m×n== members",
                "{blue:Intrinsics}: `Uppercase`, `Lowercase`, `Capitalize`, `Uncapitalize`",
                "They transform **string literal types** only"
              ],
              "style": "dot",
              "frame": "dashed",
              "ink": "green"
            },
            {
              "type": "bullets",
              "items": [
                "Combine them to build ==handler names==: `on${Capitalize<'click'>}`"
              ],
              "style": "dot"
            },
            {
              "type": "code",
              "lang": "typescript",
              "lines": [
                "type Handler = `on${Capitalize<'click'>}`;",
                "// 'onClick'"
              ],
              "note": "the standard handler-name recipe"
            },
            {
              "type": "heading",
              "text": "2. Patterns and splitting",
              "ink": "blue"
            },
            {
              "type": "table",
              "headers": [
                "Pattern",
                "Accepts"
              ],
              "rows": [
                [
                  "`${number}px`",
                  "any matching string, e.g. `'12px'`"
                ],
                [
                  "`user_${string}`",
                  "`'user_42'`, `'user_abc'`, and `'user_'`: `${string}` may be empty"
                ]
              ],
              "frame": "dashed"
            },
            {
              "type": "bullets",
              "items": [
                "Templates also work in the pattern position of `extends`",
                "In `${infer H}${infer T}`, ==H== is exactly the **first character**",
                "==T== is the **rest** of the string"
              ],
              "style": "number"
            },
            {
              "type": "code",
              "lang": "typescript",
              "lines": [
                "type Split<S> = S extends `${infer H}${infer T}`",
                "  ? [H, T] : never;",
                "// Split<'abc'> is ['a', 'bc']"
              ]
            },
            {
              "type": "callout",
              "style": "sticky",
              "title": "Remember",
              "text": "Template literal types exist only at compile time. A pattern like `${string}` accepts **any** matching string, not one fixed value."
            }
          ]
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "title": "Mapped Types and Key Remapping with as",
      "role": "outline",
      "outlineIndex": 2,
      "pages": [
        {
          "title": "Mapped Types and Key Remapping with as",
          "blocks": [
            {
              "type": "heading",
              "text": "1. Basic Form and Modifiers",
              "ink": "blue"
            },
            {
              "type": "bullets",
              "items": [
                "`type Copy<T> = { [K in keyof T]: T[K] }` is a ==homomorphic== mapped type",
                "Mapping over `keyof T` preserves **optional** and **readonly** modifiers"
              ],
              "style": "dot"
            },
            {
              "type": "table",
              "headers": [
                "Syntax",
                "Effect"
              ],
              "rows": [
                [
                  "`-?`",
                  "removes optional: builds `Required<T>`"
                ],
                [
                  "`+?`",
                  "adds optional"
                ],
                [
                  "`-readonly`",
                  "removes readonly"
                ],
                [
                  "`+readonly`",
                  "adds readonly"
                ]
              ]
            },
            {
              "type": "heading",
              "text": "2. Key Remapping with as",
              "ink": "green"
            },
            {
              "type": "bullets",
              "items": [
                "`[K in keyof T as NewKey]: T[K]` ==renames== each key",
                "Template literals build names; `K & string` is needed as keyof may include ==number== or ==symbol=="
              ],
              "style": "dot"
            },
            {
              "type": "code",
              "lang": "typescript",
              "lines": [
                "type Getters<T> = {",
                " [K in keyof T as `get${Capitalize<K & string>}`]: () => T[K]",
                "};"
              ],
              "note": "{ name: string } becomes { getName: () => string }"
            },
            {
              "type": "bullets",
              "items": [
                "Remap a key to ==never== and it is **dropped**"
              ],
              "style": "check"
            },
            {
              "type": "code",
              "lang": "typescript",
              "lines": [
                "type NoFns<T> = {",
                " [K in keyof T as T[K] extends Function ? never : K]: T[K]",
                "};"
              ]
            },
            {
              "type": "callout",
              "style": "sticky",
              "title": "Classic error",
              "text": "Skip `K & string` and `Capitalize<K>` fails: `Type 'K' does not satisfy the constraint 'string'`."
            }
          ]
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "title": "Conditional Types and infer",
      "role": "outline",
      "outlineIndex": 3,
      "pages": [
        {
          "title": "Conditional Types and infer",
          "blocks": [
            {
              "type": "heading",
              "text": "1. Assignability and Distribution",
              "ink": "green"
            },
            {
              "type": "bullets",
              "items": [
                "`T extends U ? X : Y` tests ==assignability==, not equality",
                "`string extends string | number` is {green:true}",
                "Naked parameter T ==distributes== over a union",
                "Wrap it as `[T] extends [U]` to {red:turn distribution off}"
              ],
              "style": "dot",
              "frame": "dashed",
              "ink": "green"
            },
            {
              "type": "code",
              "lang": "typescript",
              "lines": [
                "type ToArray<T> = T extends any ? T[] : never;",
                "type A = ToArray<string | number>;",
                "// string[] | number[]",
                "type B<T> = [T] extends [any] ? T[] : never;",
                "// B<string | number> is (string | number)[]"
              ],
              "note": "naked T distributes; [T] does not"
            },
            {
              "type": "callout",
              "style": "sticky",
              "title": "never",
              "text": "A naked `never` distributes over an empty union and returns ==never==. Guard with `[T] extends [never]`."
            },
            {
              "type": "heading",
              "text": "2. Extracting with infer",
              "ink": "blue"
            },
            {
              "type": "table",
              "headers": [
                "Goal",
                "Pattern"
              ],
              "rows": [
                [
                  "Return type",
                  "`T extends (...a: any[]) => infer R ? R : never`"
                ],
                [
                  "Element type",
                  "`T extends (infer E)[] ? E : T`"
                ],
                [
                  "Promise value",
                  "`T extends Promise<infer U> ? Awaited<U> : T`"
                ]
              ],
              "frame": "dashed"
            },
            {
              "type": "bullets",
              "items": [
                "The return pattern is how ==ReturnType<T>== works",
                "Several `infer` of one name in {green:covariant} slots → **union**",
                "Several in {red:contravariant} slots → **intersection**"
              ],
              "style": "check"
            }
          ]
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "title": "Common Mistakes with Type-Level Features",
      "role": "outline",
      "outlineIndex": 4,
      "pages": [
        {
          "title": "Common Mistakes with Type-Level Features",
          "blocks": [
            {
              "type": "heading",
              "text": "1. Keys and unions in strings",
              "ink": "red"
            },
            {
              "type": "code",
              "lang": "typescript",
              "lines": [
                "type Bad<T> = { [K in keyof T as `get${K}`]: T[K] }",
                "// error: Type 'symbol' is not assignable",
                "type Ok<T> = { [K in keyof T as `get${K & string}`]: T[K] }"
              ],
              "note": "keyof T may include symbol and number"
            },
            {
              "type": "bullets",
              "items": [
                "Fix: {green:`K & string`} or `Extract<keyof T, string>`",
                "Unions in each slot ==multiply== (m×n×...)",
                "Several large slots can hit the ==100,000-member== union limit or slow the compiler"
              ],
              "style": "cross",
              "ink": "red"
            },
            {
              "type": "heading",
              "text": "2. Distribution and modifiers",
              "ink": "orange"
            },
            {
              "type": "bullets",
              "items": [
                "Only a {blue:naked} parameter distributes: `T extends U`",
                "`T[] extends U` or `[T] extends U` is ==not distributed==",
                "Modifiers survive when iterating `keyof T` or a `K extends keyof T`",
                "`[K in SomeUnion]` ==loses== `?` and `readonly`; `[K in keyof T as ...]` keeps them"
              ],
              "style": "cross",
              "ink": "orange"
            },
            {
              "type": "heading",
              "text": "3. Recursion depth",
              "ink": "purple"
            },
            {
              "type": "table",
              "headers": [
                "Recursion",
                "Depth limit"
              ],
              "rows": [
                [
                  "Normal instantiation",
                  "**100**"
                ],
                [
                  "Tail-recursive conditional",
                  "up to **1000**"
                ]
              ]
            },
            {
              "type": "callout",
              "style": "sticky",
              "title": "Tail-recursive",
              "text": "The recursive call is the ==whole branch result==, with nothing wrapped around it. Otherwise: 'Type instantiation is excessively deep'."
            }
          ]
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "title": "Cheat Sheet: Template, Mapped and Conditional Types",
      "role": "outline",
      "outlineIndex": 5,
      "pages": [
        {
          "title": "Cheat Sheet: Template, Mapped and Conditional Types",
          "blocks": [
            {
              "type": "heading",
              "text": "1. Strings",
              "ink": "green"
            },
            {
              "type": "table",
              "headers": [
                "Tool",
                "Form"
              ],
              "rows": [
                [
                  "Combine",
                  "`${A}${B}` gives every combination"
                ],
                [
                  "Intrinsics",
                  "Uppercase, Lowercase, Capitalize, Uncapitalize"
                ],
                [
                  "Pattern slots",
                  "`${number}px`, `user_${string}`"
                ]
              ]
            },
            {
              "type": "heading",
              "text": "2. Mapped",
              "ink": "blue"
            },
            {
              "type": "bullets",
              "items": [
                "Loop: `{ [K in keyof T]: ... }`",
                "Modifiers: ==-?== removes optional, ==+readonly== adds it",
                "Drop a key: remap it `as never`"
              ],
              "style": "dot"
            },
            {
              "type": "code",
              "lang": "typescript",
              "lines": [
                "type Getters<T> = {",
                "  [K in keyof T as `get${Capitalize<K & string>}`]: () => T[K]",
                "}"
              ],
              "note": "remap with as"
            },
            {
              "type": "heading",
              "text": "3. Conditional and infer",
              "ink": "purple"
            },
            {
              "type": "table",
              "headers": [
                "Goal",
                "Form"
              ],
              "rows": [
                [
                  "If / else",
                  "`T extends U ? X : Y`"
                ],
                [
                  "Distributes",
                  "naked union T only"
                ],
                [
                  "Opt out",
                  "`[T] extends [U]`"
                ],
                [
                  "Return type",
                  "`T extends (...a: any[]) => infer R ? R : never`"
                ],
                [
                  "Element type",
                  "`T extends (infer E)[] ? E : T`"
                ],
                [
                  "Split string",
                  "`${infer H}${infer R}` in the extends"
                ]
              ]
            },
            {
              "type": "heading",
              "text": "4. Recipes",
              "ink": "orange"
            },
            {
              "type": "bullets",
              "items": [
                "Getters<T>: remap with a template",
                "OmitByType<T,V>: `as` the key to `never`",
                "PickByValue: `as T[K] extends V ? K : never`",
                "CamelCase<S>: recursive infer on `_`"
              ],
              "style": "check"
            },
            {
              "type": "callout",
              "style": "sticky",
              "title": "Remember",
              "text": "Use `K & string` before a key goes in a template. These types are erased at runtime."
            }
          ]
